// The app target's product identity. PRODUCT_NAME is a clean technical
// identifier (no spaces) on purpose: a spaced PRODUCT_NAME changes the
// built executable's filename too, which breaks Xcode's default TEST_HOST
// computation for hosted unit tests and Swift's default module-name
// derivation. The human-facing placeholder display name (DECISIONS 0004 —
// the app name is undecided; never the rejected name) lives in exactly one
// Swift source location instead: `AppIdentity.displayName` in
// QueerTVGuide/App/AppIdentity.swift. Renaming the app is therefore two
// edits — this identifier plus that constant — not a scattered search.
//
// Included ONLY by App.xcconfig (the app target), never by the test
// targets' config chain — every target sharing one PRODUCT_NAME collides.
PRODUCT_NAME = QueerTVGuide
PRODUCT_BUNDLE_IDENTIFIER = com.chelseakr.queertvguide
INFOPLIST_KEY_CFBundleDisplayName = $(PRODUCT_NAME)

// App Store submission keys the generated Info.plist was missing.
// - iPad multitasking needs all four orientations declared, or upload
//   validation rejects the build (the target supports iPad:
//   TARGETED_DEVICE_FAMILY = 1,2 in Shared.xcconfig). iPhone: no
//   upside-down, as Xcode's own template.
// - Export compliance: the app's one network call is HTTPS through
//   URLSession, and it contains no encryption of its own, so it uses no
//   non-exempt encryption. Declaring it here answers App Store Connect's
//   question for every build.
// - Category: Entertainment, per docs/APP-STORE.md §1.
INFOPLIST_KEY_UISupportedInterfaceOrientations_iPad = UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait UIInterfaceOrientationPortraitUpsideDown UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeLeft UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeRight
INFOPLIST_KEY_UISupportedInterfaceOrientations_iPhone = UIInterfaceOrientationPortrait UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeLeft UIInterfaceOrientationLandscapeRight
INFOPLIST_KEY_ITSAppUsesNonExemptEncryption = NO
INFOPLIST_KEY_LSApplicationCategoryType = public.app-category.entertainment
